L36: Egg Total Lipid and Phospholipid Composition
L37: Egg total fat content was not different across treatments ( P  > 0.05;  Table 3 ). Egg PC content was higher in Flax+Cho than Flax+Met ( P  < 0.05) and was not different from Control and Flax ( P  > 0.05). There was no effect of diet in egg PE, PC+PE or PC:PE was noticed among the treatments ( P  > 0.05). Table 3 Effect of methionine and choline supplementation on total lipids and phospholipid classes in egg yolk from hens fed flaxseed-based diets Table 3 Dietary treatments 1 Egg lipids Control Flax Flax+Met Flax+Cho P  value Total lipids (g/100 g) 28.10 27.11 27.75 26.73 0.201 Phosphatidylcholine (PC) (µg/mg) 47.51 b 53.51 ab 44.18 b 57.06 a 0.010 Phosphatidylethanolamine (PE) (µg/mg) 30.37 30.56 24.78 25.86 0.294 PC+PE 77.88 84.07 68.97 82.92 0.189 PC:PE 1.56 1.75 1.78 2.23 0.081 ab Means within a row with no common superscript differ significantly ( P  ≤ 0.05). 1 Control, Flax, Flax+Met, and Flax+Cho, represent corn-soybean meal basal diet containing 0% flaxseed, (Control), 15/100 g flaxseed (Flax), Flax+ 50% more Met (Flax+Met), and Flax+0.15/100 g choline chloride (Flax+Cho) respectively, n = 6.
L38: The Egg FA Composition, Lipid Peroxidation Products, and Tocopherol Content
